=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/FeedbackQueue (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/FeedbackQueue   kind=page   web route=/admin/feedback
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/FeedbackQueuePage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + maui-windows workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs
  (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7 ApiLogsPage does. The generated prompt's idealized
  "FeedbackQueuePage.xaml + FeedbackQueuePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("FeedbackQueue", already in
  RouteTable.cs → /admin/feedback).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data sources are useFeedbackList (GET /admin/feedback) + useUpdateFeedback
  (PATCH /admin/feedback/{id}). The view-model reads/writes through an injected IFeedbackQueueFeed; the default
  EmptyFeedbackQueueFeed resolves the empty state (matching the ApiLogsPage host-injection precedent), and the
  generated-client-backed FeedbackQueueClientFeed (FeedbackQueuePage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI
  contract client — GET get_api_v1_admin_feedback with snake_case status/category/limit/offset query params (unset
  filters omitted, exactly as the web buildQuery), and PATCH patch_api_v1_admin_feedback_id with the touched
  FeedbackUpdate field only — and is asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches the view.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this admin surface); timestamps format through the shared
  DateTimeFormatting port (web formatDateTime) and the reporter email is masked at the display boundary via
  TsMaskedValue (MaskVariant.Email).
- All 38 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/en/Resources.resw (translation.feedback.* + translation.common.*);
  the surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names (no new catalog rows required).
- Pre-existing blocker repaired: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been re-corrupted by its documented .gitattributes
  merge=union strategy into FOUR <Project> roots plus stranded Compile items (MSB4025), which failed XML load and
  blocked the whole-solution build at baseline. Regenerated it into the single canonical Project root the file's own
  INVARIANT mandates: case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated union of every Microsoft.UI-free
  source (1321 distinct) plus the three new FeedbackQueuePage Model/Source/ViewModel links (1324 total). No linked
  source dropped (Stale=0).

